      {
        "review_id": 555791728,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r555791728-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Moving",
        "text": "A moving and deeply symbolic place where Hindu’s clean and cremate their dead. It’s hard to explain the cultural gap between the Western sanitisation, medicalisation and hiding of death and it’s rituals: and this public, symbolic, emotional practical disposal of the dead. Surrounding this open, routine management of the end of life, the street kids smile and ask for chocolate whilst the cremated remains of citizens are swept into the holy river so that another pyre can be built. It’s not shocking, but it is thought provoking. ",
