      {
        "review_id": 555341553,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r555341553-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A Place where every Hindu wants to rest in peace !",
        "text": "Located on the bank of holy Bagmati river in Kathmandu, Nepal, the Lord Pashupatinath temple is a holy and sacred place every Hindu people worldwide. Built in Malla era, thousands year ago, it is believed that the roof of the temple is made of pure gold and walls of pure silver. In Hindu mythology, it is said that the Lord Shiv used to play and wander around this holy land including Sleshmantak forest with his beloved wife Parvati incarnating different forest animals. People cremate their deceased beloved ones on the bank of Bagmati river and on the palm of Lord Pashupatinath. It is believed that once cremate there, the deceased soul rest in peace and heaven. Nepal government has build electric crematorium nearby now to save environment and forest but people's strong belief on final rites of their beloved ones in traditional fire pyre is so strong that any one can see lines of burning pyres daily. Once you see, the burning pyre, you will be nostalgic and rethink about yourself. Many people abandon their bad and unsocial activities and changed themselves after visiting this holy place. This holy place is a home of many Sadhus as well. They are always praying for peace and prosperity around the globe. Shivaratri (birthday of Lord Shiva), Balachaturdashi and Teej (a day when mother Parvati remain on fast and beg Lord Shiva as her husband) are the main days around a year when there is a huge crowd gather to offer Lord Shiva their sacred gifts, worship and pray.\nThe main temple has four doors depicting four sides on earth and four mouth of the Lord Shiva. It is believed that the pray, worship and Arati shoud go daily without any interrupt. So Malla king started appointing the main priest from south India. At that time, it was believed that all the people in nation are the children of the king and once the kind dies, the children are automatically on sorrow and they can not worship and pray.\nOnly hindu people are allowed to enter into the holy temple premises but one can study and enjoy the atmosphere just sitting next hill to the river which is a part of Sleshmantak forest. Hundreds of small and large temples including Ram mandir and Guhyashwari temples are around the holy site.\nThe site is just a kilometer away from Tribhuvan International airport and many 3-4 star hotels are available there for domestic and international guest. ",
